# Model config: Qwen3.8-27B in INSTRUCT / non-thinking mode -- model-intrinsic.
#
# Same UD-Q8_K_XL weights as models/qwen3.8-27b-q8.env; only the sampling recipe
# differs. Qwen publishes two distinct recipes for this model and mixing them up
# is the usual cause of looping or flat output:
#
#   THINKING (default, models/qwen3.8-27b*.env):
#     temp 1.0, top-p 0.95, top-k 20, min-p 0.0, presence 0.0, repeat 1.0
#   INSTRUCT (this file):
#     temp 0.7, top-p 0.80, top-k 20, min-p 0.0, presence 1.5, repeat 1.0
#
# The presence penalty of 1.5 is deliberate and much higher than the thinking
# recipe: it is what suppresses loops when the model is not allowed to think
# first. Qwen documents it as tunable over 0..2 -- raise it if you still see
# repetition, but note high values can cause language mixing and mild quality
# loss, so back off before blaming the quant.
#
# IMPORTANT: this file sets sampling only. Thinking is ON by default in the
# chat template and CANNOT be turned off from the CLI -- the caller must send
#   chat_template_kwargs: {"enable_thinking": false}
# per request. Without that, you get thinking-mode output driven by
# instruct-mode sampling, which is the worst of both. Use this config only if
# your client sets that flag (opencode/OpenAI-compatible clients can).
#
# Everything else -- architecture, KV math, context, vision: see
# models/qwen3.8-27b.env.

: "${MODEL:=Qwen3.8-27B/Qwen3.8-27B-UD-Q8_K_XL.gguf}"

LLAMA_ARGS+=(--temp 0.7 --top-p 0.80 --top-k 20 --min-p 0.0 --presence-penalty 1.5 --repeat-penalty 1.0)
LLAMA_ARGS+=(--mmproj "/models/Qwen3.8-27B/mmproj-F16.gguf")
LLAMA_ARGS+=(--alias qwen3.8-27b-instruct)
